{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"number"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLNumberLevelV","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumberLevel","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLNumberLevel"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps to the MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"code":"number","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" attribute.","type":"text"}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNonArpeggiate\/number","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Distinguishes multiple non-arpeggiate elements on a single note."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnonarpeggiate\/number"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"number","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLNumberLevel","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLNumberLevelV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"symbolKind":"property","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Property","role":"symbol","title":"number","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL16MXLNonArpeggiateV6numberAA14MXLNumberLevelVSgvp"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNonArpeggiate"]]},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNumberLevel":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnumberlevel","role":"symbol","title":"MXLNumberLevel","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumberLevel","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLNumberLevel","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Slurs, tuplets, and many other features can be concurrent and overlap within a single musical part. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"number-level entity distinguishes up to 16 concurrent objects of the same type when the objects overlap in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"MusicXML document order. Values greater than 6 are usually only needed for music with a large number of divisi","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"staves in a single part, or if there are more than 6 cross-staff arpeggios in a single measure. When a number-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"level value is implied, the value is 1 by default.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLNumberLevel","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNonArpeggiate/number":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"number"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"text":"MXLNumberLevel","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLNumberLevelV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNonArpeggiate\/number","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Distinguishes multiple non-arpeggiate elements on a single note.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"number","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnonarpeggiate\/number"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNonArpeggiate":{"title":"MXLNonArpeggiate","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnonarpeggiate","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The non-arpeggiate type indicates that this note is at the top or bottom of a bracket indicating to not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"arpeggiate these notes. Since this does not involve playback, it is only used on the top or bottom notes, not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on each note as for the arpeggiate type."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLNonArpeggiate","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLNonArpeggiate","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNonArpeggiate"}}}